{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nI reached Amsterdam at noon, straight to Dr. Besseling, who was gracious but busy. The food at his table was competent, if dull; I paid two guilders for the meal. Later I wandered into the picture gallery. I must confess I was struck dumb by a Rembrandt, some fifteen feet wide. It is not merely a picture; it is the very air of the city. I did not finish the collection, nor do I wish to. My eyes are tired, and the light here is flat compared to Berlin’s.\n\nI think of the boys. I hope they are studying, not just idling. I have taken a room near the canal; the noise of the water is constant, a kind of restlessness. I am tired, but content. Write to me soon.\n\nYours,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795219292,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":182,"prompt_tokens":1113,"total_tokens":1295,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-cMzMVT0vkg73QBWbYz1RN83zZOKGq4bV","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1113,"prompt_ms":1086.595,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9762758310871519,"prompt_per_second":1024.3006824069687,"predicted_n":182,"predicted_ms":4263.277,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.554016574585635,"predicted_per_second":42.45560398726144}}